@startuml ws-alert-scope-filtering-classes
title Per-Connection State, Reusing CP2's Predicate (CP3)

skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam classBorderColor #888888
skinparam classBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam classHeaderBackgroundColor #DBEAFE

class ConnectionState <<one per open WebSocket, replaces the old bare connectionBBox map>> {
  role: 'operator' | 'demo'
  userId: string
  positionBBox: BBox | null
  operatorScope: ScopeFilter | null
  scopeLoaded: boolean
}

note right of ConnectionState
  positionBBox is unchanged from before CP3 --
  still drives position-updates filtering.
  operatorScope/scopeLoaded are new: loaded
  once from user_workspaces at connection open,
  for role == operator only. Demo never
  populates operatorScope -- it filters alerts
  from positionBBox instead, at delivery time.
end note

class ScopeFilter <<from CP2, unchanged>> {
  bounds: GeoBounds
  entity_types: string[] | null
  alert_types: string[] | null
}

class "matchesScope()" as Predicate <<from CP2, unchanged>> {
  (alert: AlertForScopeCheck, scope: ScopeFilter) => boolean
}

class "GET /alerts (CP2)" as RestCaller <<REST>> {
}

class "alert-events fan-out (CP3, this checkpoint)" as WsCaller <<WebSocket>> {
  operator: scope from ConnectionState.operatorScope
  demo: ephemeral ScopeFilter built\nfrom ConnectionState.positionBBox
}

ConnectionState --> ScopeFilter : operatorScope
ConnectionState --> "BBox" : positionBBox
RestCaller ..> Predicate : calls
WsCaller ..> Predicate : calls
WsCaller ..> ScopeFilter : builds (from saved scope\nor ephemeral bbox)

note bottom of WsCaller
  Nothing about matchesScope changed for CP3.
  The only new code is what builds a ScopeFilter
  and when -- once per connection for an operator,
  freshly from positionBBox on every alert for demo.
end note

@enduml
